sensor: npm13xx_charger: stop the charger before configuring it

The nPM1300 datasheet requires the charger to be disabled while
BCHGISETMSB/LSB change: the setting takes effect when charging is enabled.
The charger can already be on when the driver starts, because the PMIC
keeps its state across a reset of the host, or because a bootloader enabled
it. The driver's writes then have no effect on the current: charging goes on
at the old value while IBAT readings are converted using the new one.

Seen on the Framework Control Board: on a cold boot the registers read
BCHGISET 60/0 (240 mA) with charging enabled before the driver starts. With
450 mA in devicetree it delivered about 240 mA and readings were 1.9 times
too high. With this change it delivers 0.44 A on a meter (0.50 A read),
0.48 A is drawn from USB instead of 0.27 A, and in constant voltage a meter
shows 78 mA against 78-81 mA read.

Applies to FrameworkComputer/zephyr 8597b2f.

diff --git a/drivers/sensor/nordic/npm13xx_charger/npm13xx_charger.c b/drivers/sensor/nordic/npm13xx_charger/npm13xx_charger.c
--- a/drivers/sensor/nordic/npm13xx_charger/npm13xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/sensor/nordic/npm13xx_charger/npm13xx_charger.c
@@ -536,6 +536,14 @@ int npm13xx_charger_init(const struct device *dev)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}

+	/* The charge current takes effect when charging is enabled, and the charger
+	 * may still be on from before a reset of the host, so stop it first.
+	 */
+	ret = mfd_npm13xx_reg_write(config->mfd, CHGR_BASE, CHGR_OFFSET_EN_CLR, 1U);
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	/* Configure temperature thresholds */
 	ret = mfd_npm13xx_reg_write(config->mfd, ADC_BASE, ADC_OFFSET_NTCR_SEL,
 				    config->thermistor_idx);
